export const body = "<p>This article shares his experience on game art design. Through his piece called \"SPECIMEN,\" Chris introduces design principles and tips to improve comprehension, as well as a breakdown of lighting, composition, and overpainting.</p>\n\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/565deaab41966e0d27d3.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/565deaab41966e0d27d3.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"495\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 1\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/eea70139315984cd1797.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/eea70139315984cd1797.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"491\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 2\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/c23c2d8298c4023e3f7c.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/c23c2d8298c4023e3f7c.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"492\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 3\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<h2>Design principles</h2>\n\n<p>There are several principles that artists can mix and match for their artwork. SPECIMEN uses symmetry, contrast, repetition, similarity, ratio, and weight. Of these principles, balance is the most prominent one. For example, these 3 cylinders look balanced despite having various contents, thanks to their symmetrical position and appearance.</p>\n\n<p>The second principle here is big-medium-small. A 30/70 ratio was applied for all big and small shapes, including the glass, the hard surface at the bottom, the container, the content, or the decals/labels to the white lower hard surface. You can also break it down further, like 70% big shapes, 25% medium shape and 5% small shapes. This ratio is affected by the art style.</p>\n\n<p>The third principle, similarity, makes the contents fit together like a unit. If you look closely at the left cylinder, you will notice that 3 life forms in it have the same silhouette. Similarly, the right cylinder has three rocks with different sizes but same color and silhouette.</p>\n\n<p>Contrast is another important element, including color, brightness, and shape. Three containers are similar, with straight edges and plain color. Meanwhile, the contents are variable in shape, color, and material. The spindly creatures, colorful flower, and uneven rocks stand out against the uniform cylinders.</p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/e9719d57cb443ae8c245.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/e9719d57cb443ae8c245.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"495\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 4\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/881574fd6deb30a3c4cd.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/881574fd6deb30a3c4cd.webp\" width=\"1103\" height=\"547\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 5\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/2f726a3d2cbc66d08a6a.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/2f726a3d2cbc66d08a6a.webp\" width=\"1102\" height=\"546\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 6\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<h2>Lighting breakdown</h2>\n\n<p>For props that aren’t too reliant on sunlight, shadows, and volumetrics, the artist applied a three-point lighting setup to them. This setup includes a key light (the main light source), a fill light (the side light source), and a rim light (the light source from behind). You can add, reduce, or change the intensities of those lights as you see fit.</p>\n\n<p>The lighting process has 5 steps.</p>\n\n<p>Step 1: There is light within each tub to illuminate the objects inside, so the artist didn't need many lights for the scene.</p>\n\n<p>Step 2: Small and soft key light coming from the front and above behind the camera to show the non-glassy parts of the cylinders.</p>\n\n<p>Step 3: Big overhead light to illuminate the details of objects inside, including roughness, texture, reflections, and the plastic bases of the tubes.</p>\n\n<p>Step 4: Two rim lights behind the cylinder to pick up the edges of the tubes, add some reflections and highlight the shinier parts of the reflective materials.</p>\n\n<p>Step 5: Environment light that comes from the light reacting to the surface makes the objects more believable, especially the reflections of parts of the floor in glass and droplets.</p>\n\n<p>To save time, you can also use HDRI to create the natural feeling. However, based on the characteristics of your renderer, you will have to adjust HDRI, which takes more time and effort.</p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/255a3eec61e76e6eca50.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/255a3eec61e76e6eca50.webp\" width=\"943\" height=\"918\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 7\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/23d13d4074d2a6f3ff77.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/23d13d4074d2a6f3ff77.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"492\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 8\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p>For this piece, the lighting evolved alongside the modelling. Knowing he would place glass cylinders against a blank space from the get-go, the artist factored lighting in his creative process early on. Besides, this concept didn't rely heavily on mood, so the lighting was mainly practical. If your concept needs to evoke a certain mood, you may want to plan your lighting even earlier.</p>\n\n<p>The opposite picture shows an earlier version of SPECIMEN which has a bright environment. This idea was scraped since the contrast was too low to emphasize the tubes.</p>\n\n<h2>Creating the contents</h2>\n\n<p>Objects in the containers aren't created from scratch. For the flower in the middle container, the artist combined two 3D scans of a succulent to make it look like an alien plant. To create the spiders on the left, he used humanoid models, but adjusted the bones and rigs to mimic the spider appearance. The boulders on the right are just simply made of a rock model.</p>\n\n<p>The composition for this scene is quite straightforward. the artist wanted to give all three cylinders the same exposure, so he chose the straight frontal perspective. However, his piece violates the rule of thirds overlay as the cylinders are a bit to the right side. He intended to do so as he would give his concept some UI overlay afterwards.</p>\n\n<p>This UI overlay is slightly on the left to correct the mismatch of the right-side oriented objects. It’s more like the artist’s personal preference, but it leads to a pleasing outcome.</p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/ef8691d3f0e006fb0363.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/ef8691d3f0e006fb0363.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"485\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 9\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/dd759b72a995d8d3b3fc.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/dd759b72a995d8d3b3fc.webp\" width=\"1105\" height=\"547\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 10\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/f5047f763998b613358e.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/f5047f763998b613358e.webp\" width=\"1100\" height=\"545\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 11\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/fc74880c5d2e996a8b17.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/fc74880c5d2e996a8b17.webp\" width=\"1101\" height=\"546\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 12\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p>A common composition mistake is showing too much detail. A good composition is one that has a clear focal point and supporting elements around it. Therefore, choose your point of interest and make it the focus.</p>\n\n<p>The opposite pictures was an old exercise of the artist. For this piece, he used rough geometry and focused on mood and composition. Therefore, the light and mood were the most important element, intentionally leaving the geometry and textures unrefined.</p>\n\n<h2>Fogged glass</h2>\n\n<p>He mainly used Blender to create fogged acrylic glass. He turned up the transmission in BSDF shader and adjusted IOR (Index of Refraction) of 1.490. IOR stores the light refraction information and shows to the shader.</p>\n\n<p>Then he gave all the cylinders a roughness map. The shader creates fogged glass based on each cylinder and roughness map setup.</p>\n\n<p>For the first cylinder, he made the bottom foggier than the top by giving the roughness map a smooth transition to make the top slightly darker than the bottom. Combining with the pre-made moisture effect, he managed to create the droplets running down the glass.</p>\n\n<p>The second cylinder is the inverted version of the first one. the artist gave the water droplets more roughness so that they can reflect more of the environment, makes them look like water. Then he quickly finished the glass by adding a bit of smudges.</p>\n\n<p>The artist skipped the rough map for the final cylinder because he knew he would paint it over with some smudges later. Adding more smudges, fingerprints or small dust particles to the map is optional.</p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/d5227428a22aa29fe984.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/d5227428a22aa29fe984.webp\" width=\"1102\" height=\"545\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 13\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/6fcf4811bec32c6863ec.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/6fcf4811bec32c6863ec.webp\" width=\"1150\" height=\"494\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 14\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/ab8f063f71dbb821bf48.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/ab8f063f71dbb821bf48.webp\" width=\"1101\" height=\"544\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 15\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/d83f7e969ce4e6a2fd6d.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/d83f7e969ce4e6a2fd6d.webp\" width=\"1098\" height=\"916\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 16\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p>Overpainting is the refining steps in which artists focus on enhancing the visual quality. They can repaint, add more details and decals, correct the lighting, or even change the concept to bring out a finalized product.</p>\n\n<p>For SPECIMEN, the artist didn’t overpaint much, he just corrected the color and values, and improve the contrast by bringing up the whites and bringing down the blacks. He then used Camera Raw Filter in Photoshop for color correcting, making use of its variable settings and smart layer. To further increase the black and white contrast, he pushed the clarity to have more sharpness. He also improved the vibrancy of the flower in the middle to make it stand out from other elements.</p>\n\n<p>Artists can also adjust a little more, by using the sharpening details to improve the edge, creating a crisper look. Adding a grain and lens correction to imitate a real-life camera is also recommended. Chromatic aberration, for example, depending on the setting, can shift the colors slightly in their opposite direction.</p>\n\n<p>However, these adjustments must not be overdone as they can lead to extreme details, colors, sharpening or contrast. Grain and lens correction may give the image too much aberration.</p>\n\n<p>After overpainting, you should compare the final product with the raw-rendered version to figure out the difference and recall the methods.</p>\n\n<h2>Tips for improvements</h2>\n\n<p>In the artist’s experience, visual library is the biggest factor to improve. While browsing, you should pay attention to the art style and the uniqueness of the piece, and how other artists solve their own problems. Other than that, implementing art fundamentals can also enhance the consistency of your art.</p>\n\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/1942264252fc49d2f17f.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/1942264252fc49d2f17f.webp\" width=\"669\" height=\"701\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 17\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>\n\n<p><a class=\"source-figure\" href=\"assets/cookies-inline/e0ef18cf94213593577a.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"assets/cookies-inline/e0ef18cf94213593577a.webp\" width=\"750\" height=\"703\" style=\"--source-width:566px\" alt=\"Illustration 18\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a></p>";
export const images = ["assets/cookies-inline/1942264252fc49d2f17f.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/23d13d4074d2a6f3ff77.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/255a3eec61e76e6eca50.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/2f726a3d2cbc66d08a6a.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/565deaab41966e0d27d3.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/6fcf4811bec32c6863ec.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/881574fd6deb30a3c4cd.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/ab8f063f71dbb821bf48.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/c23c2d8298c4023e3f7c.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/d5227428a22aa29fe984.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/d83f7e969ce4e6a2fd6d.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/dd759b72a995d8d3b3fc.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/e0ef18cf94213593577a.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/e9719d57cb443ae8c245.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/eea70139315984cd1797.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/ef8691d3f0e006fb0363.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/f5047f763998b613358e.webp", "assets/cookies-inline/fc74880c5d2e996a8b17.webp"];
